      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled metformin dose. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal function.\n\nThis may be a transposition or a total-daily-dose mix-up. Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg/day total.** This could be 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg per dose.** These are other common strengths.\n\nPlease tell me the dose and frequency you intended. If you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, confirm that and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional. I'd still advise against it."
